  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 4. A ray of light is incident on AB side of a prism (front face ABC)
    and emerges from face BC. The angle of the prism, in this case, would be
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: "In this case, the refraction first takes place at AB and then
    at BC, so the angle of the prism is the angle between AB and BC which is 45\xB0."
  options:
  - "90\xB0"
  - "45\xB0"
  - "115\xB0"
  - None of the above
  correctOptionIndex: 1
